==English==

===Etymology===
[[poly-]] + [[domino|(d)omino]], as if the ''d'' were for [[di-]], two, a domino being made up of two squares

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|s|es}}

# {{lb|en|geometry}} A [[polyform]] made by joining one or more [[square]]s edge to edge in various [[arrangement]]s.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|n-omino|''n''-omino}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|monomino}} (1 square)
* {{l|en|domino}} (2 squares)
* {{l|en|triomino}}, {{l|en|tromino}} (3 squares)
* {{l|en|tetromino}} (4 squares)
* {{l|en|pentomino}} (5 squares)
* {{l|en|hexomino}} (6 squares)
* {{l|en|heptomino}} (7 squares)
* {{l|en|octomino}} (8 squares)
* {{l|en|nonomino}} (9 squares)
* {{l|en|decomino}} (10 squares)

